  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 1.8511666666666666,
      "text": "You're making a snack mix.",
      "source_sha256": "edf790ea64cb589cf8f22e287b1581b90e1656c4a6ed9048b4174b82aaa170d5"
    },
    {
      "start": 1.9711666666666667,
      "end": 5.978833333333333,
      "text": "One scoop fills half a cup, and another fills a quarter of a cup.",
      "source_sha256": "877e6fd73c89279da5d342449b467ca69ccb4427f4d4e897b2e8704c235c4c27"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.098833333333333,
      "end": 9.613625,
      "text": "Will they fill the cup, spill over, or leave some space?",
      "source_sha256": "0b42611b7ee9cacd8541e0e37884d57390e60c52afd283e19d8212eea48fdf34"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.333333333333334,
      "end": 16.4505,
      "text": "Today, we're learning to add and subtract fractions using visual models and number strategies.",
      "source_sha256": "63f3879208eba89c197f74e369b1b334b839eead73ef86bc006e7e49f6ed6e3f"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.5705,
      "end": 20.057166666666667,
      "text": "The secret is working with equal-sized parts.",
      "source_sha256": "c45f5cd9ea58f930319154607971d0d38513511e7df53b99f5abe8e68a2f3d5b"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.666666666666668,
      "end": 25.003833333333333,
      "text": "You'll make the parts the same size when the denominators are related.",
      "source_sha256": "45416ae69a5bba121030dee05a97944d3cc7df2d97a96e782022f2b7f25b681e"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.233333333333334,
      "end": 29.828958333333333,
      "text": "You'll add or subtract carefully, and simplify your answer when you can.",
      "source_sha256": "7c646e56d59df31897bd9894bd292877ba97fd474775cd36564e0c350717ca91"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.033333333333335,
      "end": 35.547,
      "text": "You'll use a model, a number line or an estimate to explain why your answer makes sense.",
      "source_sha256": "e06f90164878a6e22ab0445bfc3fbffe0e6ca9f7e6faee7e3146fce386563448"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.766666666666666,
      "end": 37.331,
      "text": "First, choose one whole.",
      "source_sha256": "c95935f98dca4dbd6067be9fc5d3ffe57fe52652d18f182cf155e206cf41e492"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.451,
      "end": 40.16725,
      "text": "Its parts must be equal in size.",
      "source_sha256": "ae991533b6ad658dde26876d25212a27aa8c91dab88ba94fe7b2dd6902ab5c48"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.28725,
      "end": 44.924458333333334,
      "text": "The outline of the model shows the entire whole, not just the coloured share.",
      "source_sha256": "d6abbd24c39758b034466b468b623de477e886ac9cb4c93c0baa3670c56754c5"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.43333333333333,
      "end": 48.64879166666667,
      "text": "Here, three equal parts are chosen out of four.",
      "source_sha256": "63f4310cac29388f9178d90c1790c7d787f80ea7516e188992feec5ca2796696"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.768791666666665,
      "end": 52.537791666666664,
      "text": "The top number, the numerator, counts chosen parts.",
      "source_sha256": "ec4b28360490b06d5a705b1c1ff8d6563a5374da389288ba01ffa8e1e841f720"
    },
    {
      "start": 52.65779166666667,
      "end": 57.273208333333336,
      "text": "The bottom number, the denominator, tells how many equal parts make the whole.",
      "source_sha256": "fb01afef746abdbb770b06205fdd64bd18bcd6d7cb820f6a5ef2846567907391"
    },
    {
      "start": 57.9,
      "end": 60.592708333333334,
      "text": "What is two sevenths plus three sevenths?",
      "source_sha256": "d55fbaee26f48219be686d2f64c94d6a961163e49594acccf0fd9079b764df55"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.71270833333333,
      "end": 65.63904166666667,
      "text": "Think about the size of each piece, then predict the number of pieces altogether.",
      "source_sha256": "e45066aaf9e9c280dd5aec43149eac06fbf553cd6c43d8d83fba5d2a18bee2f1"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.66666666666667,
      "end": 71.32058333333333,
      "text": "First, use matching denominators.",
      "source_sha256": "bb8b03d7875be74206ce84e77a34963b3129f23abc21d67d0599b7131c6a5853"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.44058333333334,
      "end": 74.97416666666666,
      "text": "Two sevenths plus three sevenths makes five sevenths.",
      "source_sha256": "0be1700bc4552efcb661e9ed59c9ff69a255743deb9660bd20cf9aa536998630"
    },
    {
      "start": 75.33333333333333,
      "end": 78.59179166666667,
      "text": "We add the numerators and keep the denominator.",
      "source_sha256": "576043cbbd2d5dcd4c2ce6712134950621954a25e77e1b47a8443f665766097c"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.71179166666667,
      "end": 82.21554166666667,
      "text": "We are still counting sevenths, not fourteenths.",
      "source_sha256": "32185714944166e46f6e3194937037d75350c9e026e6530251310b9601e841bd"
    },
    {
      "start": 82.56666666666666,
      "end": 88.97741666666667,
      "text": "Adding denominators would rename our pieces as fourteenths, even though we never cut the pieces smaller.",
      "source_sha256": "48594c31d2f6cb4006f3e5ffea5eb2c1acc3a7fc09f08f7d060181da86149670"
    },
    {
      "start": 89.09741666666666,
      "end": 92.59329166666667,
      "text": "Keep the piece size, and count the chosen pieces.",
      "source_sha256": "116d9877c541a7e29f3933475d4b955fdedaab2c8e624f451fcb9cc34f574112"
    },
    {
      "start": 93.26666666666667,
      "end": 98.708875,
      "text": "For half a cup plus a quarter of a cup, what size of piece could you use for both amounts?",
      "source_sha256": "94fc495db0930e332e0da60e64836143b63e6eefa24351b0261e509dd9b47caa"
    },
    {
      "start": 98.828875,
      "end": 100.28425,
      "text": "Predict the total.",
      "source_sha256": "3066f90e0857e0bd0bc6ba925cc113d8bf901b439207a3a0d543eed0f82a51a4"
    },
    {
      "start": 103.3,
      "end": 108.719,
      "text": "For one half plus one quarter, the denominators are related: four is a multiple of two.",
      "source_sha256": "c930b406ecc50adaaa01a9b4d4418d2ce0a4b084d8b5bd9243b2cc24848e0d6e"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.839,
      "end": 111.29645833333333,
      "text": "Rename the half as two quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "2963e621aac30550689990433fd700c6190cbe3d76fb9e17562e1219022a02d6"
    },
    {
      "start": 111.66666666666667,
      "end": 114.385,
      "text": "Now add two quarters and one quarter.",
      "source_sha256": "9ec1209f5e9e5c8d4703ae25354a9a0c853c3ee44857234f38c3bdae9c54289c"
    },
    {
      "start": 114.505,
      "end": 116.8335,
      "text": "The result is three quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "a39a74308110a1158d9f504ce91fa6eba59e5dc8cdfc41b6054f2e7e1be4fe0a"
    },
    {
      "start": 117.2,
      "end": 120.44566666666667,
      "text": "Two quarters plus one quarter is three quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "1fce2bb92eee5200387903c33586f5fe09dc882d882b03c008306580af0d2db6"
    },
    {
      "start": 120.56566666666667,
      "end": 125.39670833333334,
      "text": "That's more than half a cup but less than a full cup, which agrees with the picture.",
      "source_sha256": "8a460ecad41f7b0cd86ecba7d8fd5fa79948fd4f3dfcb843a768c83acddc14da"
    },
    {
      "start": 126.06666666666666,
      "end": 128.94208333333333,
      "text": "Subtraction follows the same idea.",
      "source_sha256": "6698a9f6afabd7e64868b6b0e204520557c21d8f40d3ac3c11bac144808e2b31"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.06208333333333,
      "end": 133.90158333333332,
      "text": "For three quarters minus one eighth, rename three quarters as six eighths.",
      "source_sha256": "76464a5e665978fa3525e77b925a1cb7ab5c454c0576499356a75acfc5d1c138"
    },
    {
      "start": 134.26666666666668,
      "end": 136.12454166666666,
      "text": "Take away one eighth.",
      "source_sha256": "1c1af3b9ddfa6dd34af1fb8a4f1f73c8cae565d34b5b588b9335a546f768e0d4"
    },
    {
      "start": 136.24454166666666,
      "end": 137.89266666666666,
      "text": "Five eighths remain.",
      "source_sha256": "82dffb4cb8a7ba7848e4eb07dcbe149460c39a07d31ebd852579c36ee4a3a367"
    },
    {
      "start": 138.01266666666666,
      "end": 140.16766666666666,
      "text": "The denominator stays eight.",
      "source_sha256": "91781cfcf4eb352a34717725b5aa624536bd9a0064e7b1bc57d25bc3e946425f"
    },
    {
      "start": 140.53333333333333,
      "end": 144.3995,
      "text": "Six eighths with one eighth removed leaves five eighths.",
      "source_sha256": "4870c5a7b908bc8090c0052921c1b629433eb5008e306654c059613a5b6d0113"
    },
    {
      "start": 144.5195,
      "end": 149.835625,
      "text": "The result is smaller than three quarters, so our subtraction passes a quick sense check.",
      "source_sha256": "922b4a5703e1581417c304bff5e4518ef5f6a9e80ef14e60abf3d8ae15bfa6d7"
    },
    {
      "start": 150.5,
      "end": 154.47758333333334,
      "text": "On a number line, begin at six eighths and move back one eighth.",
      "source_sha256": "86d250de786c3e3080b51674763bdea00f696c03ce25be0e1bd3cfe7a9dff112"
    },
    {
      "start": 154.59758333333335,
      "end": 156.64866666666666,
      "text": "You land on five eighths.",
      "source_sha256": "7df7caa11a98fd6a55aecd6c657f85ce15fc11c509f70d04689026e67541ae51"
    },
    {
      "start": 157.0,
      "end": 158.93395833333332,
      "text": "Simplify when you can.",
      "source_sha256": "6cd73940c7ff3c7e35391a09bdb15913f1f40acab14b434cabd18515362816eb"
    },
    {
      "start": 159.05395833333333,
      "end": 163.91125,
      "text": "One sixth plus three sixths is four sixths, which equals two thirds.",
      "source_sha256": "96bcbe801822e24c80891d14dbc0144774ef81822ddb94d8e7519ab95504c02b"
    },
    {
      "start": 164.26666666666668,
      "end": 166.733875,
      "text": "Mixed numbers can make another whole.",
      "source_sha256": "0bbff7d8c429fc95087575eb0bfa1d46c92b0344300d1246f15fdd674ac6eb71"
    },
    {
      "start": 166.853875,
      "end": 170.99733333333333,
      "text": "One and four fifths plus two fifths is one and six fifths.",
      "source_sha256": "858fe4942d8c1cce73c68ed10d5cca78adf21f4948f4742220b7b73c444b41a7"
    },
    {
      "start": 171.36666666666667,
      "end": 173.91666666666666,
      "text": "Regroup five fifths as one whole.",
      "source_sha256": "e49027dfbfdf94988e8690c95e9aca5ebee44ca3292f79776775b5b63b25bd9e"
    },
    {
      "start": 174.03666666666666,
      "end": 176.683625,
      "text": "The answer is two and one fifth.",
      "source_sha256": "c088e1d43b736b2efd4cb37d7c319aea26ef2ed0fe8377e2c67bbb1b38593aa0"
    },
    {
      "start": 177.06666666666666,
      "end": 180.97004166666667,
      "text": "For several fractions, rename them with a common denominator.",
      "source_sha256": "62b0ac0e8dcf066fc1acc5c2a9575c24c0402f88d758fb589b8c07c138a921fd"
    },
    {
      "start": 181.09004166666668,
      "end": 187.404875,
      "text": "One half plus one quarter minus one eighth becomes four eighths plus two eighths minus one eighth.",
      "source_sha256": "318adee6f9a07bf1d3034c7ea85b58fbb2e7b989b19e03f035cc4c218b559f70"
    },
    {
      "start": 187.76666666666668,
      "end": 192.32766666666666,
      "text": "Four plus two minus one is five, so the result is five eighths.",
      "source_sha256": "90395cb3f5e74a8d807ab02cf85cd79828e9d94a767de01517ccd33226f62fea"
    },
    {
      "start": 192.7,
      "end": 195.53954166666668,
      "text": "What is two thirds minus one sixth?",
      "source_sha256": "c563f49e9b0faa7819168356d3f2c2c7d6d0f2d915616a1f6168159fefbf56ca"
    },
    {
      "start": 200.56666666666666,
      "end": 202.68208333333334,
      "text": "Two thirds is four sixths.",
      "source_sha256": "ee9142fa3e7438df6d59f19b1d39430b36b2d2c98428344a937ce2f9b9a4ff07"
    },
    {
      "start": 202.80208333333334,
      "end": 207.009875,
      "text": "Four sixths minus one sixth is three sixths, or one half.",
      "source_sha256": "6ef537be91c57cd559ea6b59cd0100c19ccb9a426810c5738af9067197dfbac0"
    },
    {
      "start": 207.36666666666667,
      "end": 210.605125,
      "text": "Our goal was to add and subtract fractions.",
      "source_sha256": "c08428b3737baab784b8a120f6eeb6c5cd0ef68ada127ae3181a136aeab3ab3c"
    },
    {
      "start": 210.725125,
      "end": 215.41883333333334,
      "text": "Make the parts match, combine or remove them, then simplify and check.",
      "source_sha256": "edce9bfa18152c6e86b0533375b0018784a24066a2a0409f0a4899946b8e20d4"
    },
    {
      "start": 215.53883333333334,
      "end": 218.83479166666666,
      "text": "What would you draw first for your next calculation?",
      "source_sha256": "bff7b8c2d6db6c384662e090dfeb08fbce3c431a71f41341eee73613dc18ed46"
    },
    {
      "start": 218.95479166666667,
      "end": 221.95483333333334,
      "text": "Try the fraction practice on Math Magic.",
      "source_sha256": "7c480f83723e89b7ed1b0b2fa1aa59276b928f08100d741919b63b2b1727e157"
    },
    {
      "start": 222.07483333333334,
      "end": 226.25475,
      "text": "The separate L C M video is optional extension work.",
      "source_sha256": "1fb3de22a6f2b2ff73bc5caa36cc8331d630fbde54fbc44e53f3db1cc200ab7e"
    }
  ],
